hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
2926,"Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to me Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and 'Ata', on the authority of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (RA), who said:\n\nThe people began to talk a great deal, so we set out as pilgrims until there remained between us and the end of the ihram (ihram exit) only a few nights. Then someone said, \We have been commanded to end our ihram.\"" So one of us would go to 'Arafah with his private parts dripping with semen. This reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," so he stood up to deliver a sermon and said:\n\n\""O people", do you inform me about Allah? By Allah, I know Allah better than you and I fear Him more than you. If I were to go back to the beginning of my affair, I would not have brought sacrificial animals with me, and I would have ended my ihram just as they have ended theirs. So whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him fast three days during the Hajj and seven when he returns to his family. And whoever has a sacrificial animal with him," let him slaughter it.\""\n\nWe used to slaughter a camel on behalf of seven people.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
2927,"'Ata' said: Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) distributed sheep among his companions on that day, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas received a goat, which he slaughtered for himself. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood at 'Arafah, he ordered Rabi'ah ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf to stand beneath the belly of his she-camel. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Cry out to the people: 'Do you know which month this is?'"" They said: ""The sacred month."" He said: ""Do you know which land this is?"" They said: ""The sacred land."" He said: ""Do you know which day this is?"" They said: ""The day of the Greater Hajj."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has made your blood, your wealth, and your honor inviolable to you, like the sanctity of this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours, like the sanctity of this day of yours."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) completed his Hajj. When he stood at 'Arafah, he said: ""This is the standing place, and all of 'Arafah is a standing place."" And when he stood at Quzah, he said: ""This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.""", the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) distributed some sheep among his companions. Sa'd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (RA) received a ram, so he slaughtered it for himself. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stopped at 'Arafah, he commanded Rabī'ah ibn Ummayyah ibn Khalaf to stand beneath the udder of his she-camel. The Prophet (ﷺ) then said to him:\n'Proclaim, O people! Do you know what month this is?'\nThey said: 'The sacred month.'\nHe said: 'Do you know what land this is?'\nThey said: 'The sacred land.'\nHe said: 'Do you know what day this is?'\nThey said: 'The day of the greatest Hajj.'\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed, Allah has made your lives, your wealth, and your honor as sacred to you as this month of yours, this land of yours, and this day of yours.'\nThen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) completed his Hajj. When he stopped at 'Arafah, he said: 'This is the standing place; all of 'Arafah is a standing place.'\nAnd when he stopped at Muzdalifah," he said: 'This is the standing place; all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.'\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
